explore_lite: frontier search walks through inflated (but passable) cells

Applies to: src/third_party/m-explore-ros2 at commit 326cf8a
Applied by: patches/apply_patches.sh (run_sim.sh calls it, and rebuilds
            explore_lite when the patched source is newer than the build)

Why
---
FrontierSearch::searchFrom() does a breadth-first search from the robot's
nearest free cell, but only steps to a neighbour whose cost is <= the current
cell's cost. Starting on a free cell (cost 0) that means it only ever crosses
cost-0 cells: every inflated cell (cost 1-252) acts like a wall.

With our inflation (inflation_radius 0.35 m), a cell is cost 0 only when it is
more than 0.35 m from every obstacle. A 1.0 m doorway then has a cost-0 strip
of about 0.30 m, a 0.9 m doorway about 0.20 m, and slightly thick stereo door
frames or one stray obstacle speck closes it completely. The search can then
not leave the current room, frontiers behind the door become invisible, and
explore_lite reports "No frontiers found, stopping." while Nav2 (which accepts
any cost below 253) could drive through the door. Seen in the 2026-11-24 run:
exploration stopped at t=322 s on the way to a kitchen frontier.

Change
------
Also step to neighbours with cost < INSCRIBED_INFLATED_OBSTACLE (253), i.e.
every cell where the robot's centre is allowed - the same rule as the planner.
Unknown (255), lethal (254) and inscribed (253) cells still stop the search.
Frontier detection (a frontier cell still needs a cost-0 neighbour), frontier
ranking, min_frontier_size and the blacklist are unchanged.

